  "title": "Unify walking commands, evaluation capture and evidence checks",
  "summary": "The evaluator rejects traces that do not execute their declared commands. Native packs freeze the walking requirements. Versioned readers preserve historical receipts and unjudged rows. Training, navigation and judgement share one finite command bank. Explicit capture sources validate nominal and randomized motor laws. Publication checks reproduce accepted-controller values from pinned evidence, compare the complete runtime manifest and enforce package import boundaries. Numerical limits, checkpoint bytes and historical evidence remain unchanged.",
